  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "When an owner in the Caribbean and Latin America wants **brand affiliation** but still wants to preserve a stronger sense of **hotel individuality**, the brands most commonly considered are **soft-brand** or **collection** brands such as **Curio Collection by Hilton**, **Tapestry Collection by Hilton**, **Vignette Collection**, **Autograph Collection**, and **Ascend Hotel Collection**.[6][2][5]\n\nThese are the best fit because they provide global distribution and loyalty-program benefits while allowing more property-level identity than a fully standardized flag.[6][5] In the region, examples and active use cases include **Curio Collection**, **Tapestry Collection**, **LXR Hotels & Resorts**, and **Vignette Collection** on the Hilton/Hyatt side, plus **Ascend Collection** and **Radisson Individuals** on the Choice/Radisson side.[6][5][2]\n\nIf you want the shortest practical shortlist for the region, it is:\n- **Curio Collection by Hilton**[6]\n- **Tapestry Collection by Hilton**[6]\n- **Autograph Collection by Marriott**[2]\n- **Vignette Collection**[2]\n- **Ascend Hotel Collection**[5]\n- **Radisson Individuals**[5]\n\nBy contrast, more standardized full-service brands like **Marriott**, **Hilton**, **Hyatt Regency**, or **Grand Hyatt** are also present in the region, but they generally imply less individuality than collection-style brands.[3][2]",
